<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Central American University</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1965">1965</a>–</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as José Simeón Cañas Central American University, UCA</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The José Simeón Cañas Central American University is a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jesuits">Jesuit</a> university in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/san-salvador">San Salvador</a> founded in 1965. Under its rector Ignacio Ellacuría it became a leading voice for human rights and a negotiated end to the civil war. On 16 November 1989 soldiers of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/atlacatl-battalion">Atlacatl Battalion</a> murdered six Jesuit priests, including Ellacuría, with their housekeeper and her daughter on the campus.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/central-american-university.jpg" alt="Central American University" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: PizzaKing13 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Entrance_of_the_Central_American_University,_San_Salvador.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
